ISSUE: biomejs/biome#8094: 🐛 [lsp] Duplicate capability registrations

### Environment information

```block
CLI:
  Version:                      2.2.5
  Color support:                true

Platform:
  CPU Architecture:             aarch64
  OS:                           macos

Environment:
  BIOME_LOG_PATH:               unset
  BIOME_LOG_PREFIX_NAME:        unset
  BIOME_CONFIG_PATH:            unset
  BIOME_THREADS:                unset
  NO_COLOR:                     unset
  TERM:                         xterm-256color
  JS_RUNTIME_VERSION:           v24.5.0
  JS_RUNTIME_NAME:              node
  NODE_PACKAGE_MANAGER:         unset

Biome Configuration:
  Status:                       Not set
  Path:                         unset

Workspace:
  Open Documents:               0
```

### What happened?

There are duplicate `client/registerCapability` (and also `client/unregisterCapability`) requests triggered on starting biome lsp.

<img width="808" height="842" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/81678462-c525-4843-aa76-234ee617bf21" />

### Expected result

Either only one `client/registerCapability` request OR do the registration and registration in a proper order so that the last registration is unregistered before registering again. Currently there are two "unregisters" in a row followed by two "registers".

Depending on the client that can cause some issues. For example in Sublime Text I can see that this causes duplicate didChangeWatchedFiles notifications (again, not a huge deal but still unnecessary).

