ISSUE: evanw/esbuild#4497: CSS minifier incorrectly removes leading `&` nesting selector

The CSS minifier removes a leading `&` from nested selectors that also use `&` within other selector parts like `:not()`, which incorrectly changes the overall selector's meaning.

Reproduction: [esbuild playground](https://esbuild.github.io/try/#dAAwLjI4LjEALS1sb2FkZXI9Y3NzIC0tbWluaWZ5AC5hIHsKICAuYjpub3QoLmEgLmIgLmIpIHsKICAgIC0tbGV2ZWw6IDE7CgogICAgJiAuYjpub3QoJiAuYiAuYikgewogICAgICAtLWxldmVsOiAyOwoKICAgICAgJiAuYjpub3QoJiAuYiAuYikgewogICAgICAgIC0tbGV2ZWw6IDM7CiAgICAgIH0KICAgIH0KICB9Cn0K)

Input:

```css
.a {
  .b:not(.a .b .b) {
    --level: 1;

    & .b:not(& .b .b) {
      --level: 2;

      & .b:not(& .b .b) {
        --level: 3;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Output with esbuild 0.28.1 and `--loader=css --minify`:

```css
.a{.b:not(.a .b .b){--level:1;.b:not(& .b .b){--level:2;.b:not(& .b .b){--level:3}}}}
```

The leading `&` before each nested `.b:not(...)` selector must be preserved, or the output must be rewritten to an equivalent selector. In the example above, given three nested `.b` elements, the input computes `--level` as `1`, `2`, and `3`, while the minified output computes `3` for all three elements.

