ISSUE: ratatui/ratatui#2695: `Buffer::diff` panics with index out of bounds when a styled wide glyph in the last cell is replaced by a narrower one

## Description

`Buffer::diff` panics with an index-out-of-bounds when the **last cell of the buffer** contains a wide glyph whose style is visible on blank cells (e.g. a non-reset background), and the next frame replaces it with a narrower cell.

The "uncovered cells" force path introduced in #2587 (released in ratatui-core 0.1.2 / ratatui 0.30.2) creates its trailing range without clamping to the buffer length:

```rust
// ratatui-core/src/buffer/diff.rs:182-186
self.trailing = Some(TrailingState {
    next_index: i + 1,
    end: i + previous_width,   // <-- not clamped to `len`
    force: true,
});
```

Compare with the VS16 path a few lines above, which is clamped:

```rust
// ratatui-core/src/buffer/diff.rs:166
let trailing_end = (i + cell_width).min(len);
```

The trailing loop then indexes before it clamps:

```rust
// ratatui-core/src/buffer/diff.rs:102-108
while *next_index < *end {
    let j = *next_index;
    let cell_width = self.next[j].cell_width().max(1) as usize;  // panics when j == len
    *next_index += cell_width;
    *end = (*end).max(*next_index).min(len);                     // clamp happens too late
```

With the wide cell at `i == len - 1` and `previous_width == 2`, the range becomes `next_index = len`, `end = len + 1`, so the loop body evaluates `self.next[len]` and panics.

Because the panic fires while the diff is being consumed, it crashes the app inside `Terminal::flush` at draw time rather than at the offending write. `Buffer::set_stringn` refuses to place a wide grapheme in the last column (which is why the existing tests don't hit this), but direct cell access (`buf[pos].set_symbol(..)`) and third-party widgets reach it easily.

This is distinct from #2685 (cells skipped after a long symbol), #2652 (trailing cell not updated on style-only change), and #2651 (backend `MoveTo` handling) — this one is an out-of-bounds panic in the diff iterator itself.

## To Reproduce

```rust
use ratatui_core::buffer::Buffer;
use ratatui_core::layout::Rect;
use ratatui_core::style::Color;

fn main() {
    let rect = Rect::new(0, 0, 3, 1);
    let mut prev = Buffer::empty(rect);
    prev[(2, 0)].set_symbol("あ").set_bg(Color::Red); // wide glyph + visible bg, last cell
    let mut next = Buffer::empty(rect);
    next[(2, 0)].set_symbol("b");                     // narrower replacement

    let _ = prev.diff(&next);
    // panic: index out of bounds: the len is 3 but the index is 3
}
```

Verified against current `main` (5b016b67) and reproduces with ratatui-core 0.1.2.

A secondary effect of the same unclamped `end`: when the wide glyph sits in the last column of a *non-final* row, the trailing range spills across the row boundary and force-emits a spurious update for column 0 of the next row.

## Expected behavior

`Buffer::diff` should never index past the end of the buffer; the trailing range should be clamped to the buffer length exactly like the VS16 path (`(i + previous_width).min(len)`).

